    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1958-p25.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "By the change-of-base identity, \\[ \\log_kx\\cdot\\log_5k=\\log_5x. \\] Hence \\(\\log_5x=3,\\) so \\(x=5^3=125.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the chain identity \\(\\log_kx\\cdot\\log_5k=\\log_5x\\)",
        "Convert the resulting logarithmic equation to exponential form"
